# Competency: GMEOW must make the prose→axiom harvest PROVENANCE trace queryable in
# BOTH directions. Each row ties an accepted logic:FormalizationCandidate to the exact
# prose it was harvested from: the term (logic:candidateFormalizes), the field kind
# (logic:candidateSourceField, a closed logic:ProseField) and the annotation
# property that field stands for (logic:proseFieldProperty). Read forward — group
# by ?candidate — it answers "what prose did this candidate harvest?"; read
# inverse — filter or group by ?term / ?fieldProperty — it answers "which candidates
# were harvested from this prose field?". Only accepted candidates are canonical.
#
# This is GOVERNANCE, not the coverage MEASURE. A candidate records a reviewed
# intention to formalize; it is not itself the formalization, and this query counts
# candidates rather than realized axioms. Harvest coverage proper — the fraction of a
# slice's defined terms carrying an enforcing logic:Constraint (severity
# Violation/Warning) or a logic:Formula that logic:formalizes them — is measured by the
# gmeow:axisHarvestCoverage slice-quality axis, which deliberately does NOT count
# candidates. Read the two together: this query says what was intended and from which
# prose, the axis says what was actually realized. See docs/SLICE_QA.md.
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?candidate ?term ?field ?fieldProperty WHERE {
    ?candidate a logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
               logic:candidateLifecycle logic:CandidateAccepted ;
               logic:candidateFormalizes ?term ;
               logic:candidateSourceField ?field .
    ?field logic:proseFieldProperty ?fieldProperty .
}
ORDER BY ?candidate ?term ?field
